<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal public sector workers stage pay protest.</title>
<headline>Portugal public sector workers stage pay protest.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Several thousand public sector workers demonstrated in central Lisbon on Thursday demanding the government improve its 2.6 percent pay offer.</p>
<p>Shouting &quot;work, yes, unemployment, no,&quot; around 3,000 protesters marched to the office of Socialist Prime Minister Antonio Guterres.</p>
<p>The Communist-led Common Front union group has rejected the government's offer and is threatening strikes if the pay proposal is not improved.</p>
<p>The government says that it cannot afford wage rises significantly in excess of its 2.25-2.50 percent inflation target for next year without risking Portugal's chances of qualifing for the European Union's planned single currency.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
